WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:06.429
Robin Hood had killed a man and killed the king's deer.

2
00:00:06.489 --> 00:00:09.630
It was impossible for the young man to return home.

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:19.053
So he became an outlaw living in Sherwood Forest.

4
00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:37.806
As the year passed, one hundred outlaws joined him in the woods.

5
00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:43.689
Some of these outlaws were in trouble for shooting the king's deer because they were hungry.

6
00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.112
Other men had lost their land when the king seized it for himself.

7
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:52.834
Some men had been cheated by rich, evil bishops.

8
00:00:54.035 --> 00:00:57.337
So they were all forced to leave home and hide in the forest.

9
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:04.901
In time they chose Robin as their leader, and like Robin, they vowed to help the poor and

10
00:01:05.021 --> 00:01:05.921
people in need.

11
00:01:07.081 --> 00:01:09.642
One spring morning Robin felt restless.

12
00:01:10.802 --> 00:01:12.683
He decided to look for adventure.

13
00:01:14.063 --> 00:01:18.645
"You stay behind in the woods and listen for my horn," he said to his men.

14
00:01:18.665 --> 00:01:21.846
"If I blow it three times, come running.

15
00:01:22.646 --> 00:01:24.426
It's a signal that I need your help."

16
00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:28.568
Robin wandered out of the forest.

17
00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:33.390
He greeted pretty girls on their way to market.

18
00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:39.555
He saw a monk riding a donkey and a knight on a fine horse.

19
00:01:41.777 --> 00:01:43.718
He bowed before a fair lady.

20
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.563
At last he came to a narrow wooden bridge over a stream.

21
00:01:50.003 --> 00:01:52.665
He spotted a huge stranger on the other side.

22
00:01:53.906 --> 00:01:56.849
The narrow bridge was only wide enough for one man.

23
00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.472
Both men hurried to cross the bridge first.

24
00:02:01.952 --> 00:02:02.932
They met in the middle.

25
00:02:02.952 --> 00:02:06.073
"Out of my way!"

26
00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.194
cried Robin.

27
00:02:07.214 --> 00:02:09.674
"No," replied the stranger.

28
00:02:09.694 --> 00:02:11.775
"You get out of my way!"

29
00:02:11.795 --> 00:02:16.016
"I'll use my bow and arrows to make you move!"

30
00:02:16.396 --> 00:02:17.256
declared Robin.

31
00:02:17.276 --> 00:02:19.657
"You coward!"

32
00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:20.637
said the man.

33
00:02:20.657 --> 00:02:22.898
"You threaten me with a bow.

34
00:02:23.738 --> 00:02:25.359
But all I have is this."

35
00:02:26.419 --> 00:02:30.260
He shook a heavy wooden staff, the kind used for fighting.

36
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.141
"No one calls me a coward!"

37
00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:34.222
said Robin.

38
00:02:34.242 --> 00:02:37.503
"I'll cut a staff from those trees over there.

39
00:02:38.744 --> 00:02:40.265
Then we'll see what happens!"

40
00:02:41.165 --> 00:02:44.827
Robin stepped off the bridge and made a long staff from a tree.

41
00:02:45.488 --> 00:02:48.449
While he worked, he sneaked a look at the stranger.

42
00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:53.552
The tall man was whistling and gazing at the stream as he waited for Robin.

43
00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:55.933
"That guy is huge!"

44
00:02:56.454 --> 00:02:57.594
Robin said to himself.

45
00:02:57.614 --> 00:03:00.576
"He looks quite strong too!"

46
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.663
But Robin went bravely back to the bridge carrying his staff.

47
00:03:05.683 --> 00:03:07.545
"I'm ready.

48
00:03:08.266 --> 00:03:11.548
Let's fight on the bridge until one of us tumbles into the stream."

49
00:03:12.509 --> 00:03:15.011
The stranger twirled his staff over his head.

50
00:03:15.031 --> 00:03:16.533
"Let's go!"

51
00:03:18.635 --> 00:03:21.957
Robin struck first, but the stranger blocked the blow.

52
00:03:25.781 --> 00:03:29.244
After an hour both men were tired and bruised.

53
00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.762
At last Robin smacked the stranger in the ribs.

54
00:03:36.143 --> 00:03:38.765
The man wobbled, but didn't fall off the bridge.

55
00:03:39.365 --> 00:03:41.447
Instead he hit Robin over the head.

56
00:03:42.047 --> 00:03:43.768
Robin was furious!

57
00:03:44.268 --> 00:03:46.170
He hit the man as hard as he could.

58
00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.533
But the stranger struck back, knocking Robin into the stream.

59
00:03:53.975 --> 00:03:55.236
The stranger laughed.

60
00:03:55.256 --> 00:03:57.978
"And where are you now?"

61
00:03:59.299 --> 00:04:00.920
Robin couldn't help laughing too.

62
00:04:02.392 --> 00:04:04.233
"I'm floating out to sea!"

63
00:04:04.253 --> 00:04:06.993
he joked as he climbed onto dry land.

64
00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:08.734
"Let's shake hands.

65
00:04:09.054 --> 00:04:10.955
You're the bravest man I've ever met!"

66
00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:14.456
Robin raised his horn and blew three times.

67
00:04:15.496 --> 00:04:18.997
Suddenly a group of men dressed in green burst from the woods.

68
00:04:19.017 --> 00:04:21.918
"What's wrong, Robin?"

69
00:04:22.318 --> 00:04:23.318
called Will Scarlet.

70
00:04:23.338 --> 00:04:24.679
"You're soaking wet."

71
00:04:25.579 --> 00:04:26.379
Robin grinned.

72
00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:29.480
"This big fellow knocked me into the water."

73
00:04:30.528 --> 00:04:32.229
"Then he shall go for a swim too!"

74
00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:33.330
cried Will.

75
00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.171
Robin's men leaped onto the stranger.

76
00:04:37.272 --> 00:04:41.534
The stranger fought back fiercely with his staff, but they wrestled him to the ground.

77
00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:44.836
"Let him go!"

78
00:04:45.196 --> 00:04:45.817
Robin said.

79
00:04:45.837 --> 00:04:47.058
"Don't hurt him.

80
00:04:47.658 --> 00:04:49.639
He seems like a good and honest man."

81
00:04:50.399 --> 00:04:54.262
Then he said to the stranger, "How about joining my band of men?

82
00:04:55.562 --> 00:04:58.104
You'll have three suits of green clothes every year.

83
00:04:58.892 --> 00:05:00.613
Plus, all you can eat and drink."

84
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:05.056
"You're not very good with a staff," grumbled the man.

85
00:05:06.076 --> 00:05:08.037
He was still angry with Robin's men.

86
00:05:08.057 --> 00:05:11.039
"Can you shoot an arrow better than I can?

87
00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:14.201
If so, then I'll join you."

88
00:05:14.221 --> 00:05:16.682
"Fine!" said Robin.

89
00:05:16.702 --> 00:05:19.444
"Someone lend this stranger a bow and arrow."

90
00:05:20.644 --> 00:05:24.526
Will cut a small piece of white bark and fastened it to a tree.

91
00:05:25.387 --> 00:05:26.427
The stranger took aim.

92
00:05:27.596 --> 00:05:29.657
He hit the bark with his first arrow.

93
00:05:29.677 --> 00:05:32.539
"Nice shot," Robin said.

94
00:05:32.559 --> 00:05:35.020
"Now it is my turn."

95
00:05:35.881 --> 00:05:37.501
Robin stepped up and aimed.

96
00:05:38.822 --> 00:05:43.044
His arrow cut through the air—and split the first arrow down the middle!

97
00:05:43.064 --> 00:05:46.686
"What an incredible shot!"

98
00:05:47.187 --> 00:05:48.067
cried the stranger.

99
00:05:48.087 --> 00:05:52.490
"I'm John Little, and I'll gladly join your band."

100
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:54.351
Robin grinned.

101
00:05:54.371 --> 00:05:59.378
"You're such a big man—I think we'll call you Little John.

102
00:06:00.822 --> 00:06:04.471
My name is Robin Hood, and you shall be my right-hand man."
